<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6335" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calvārĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		calva, calvus. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The skull</i> of man, <i><span class="en">Cels. 8,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 4 Reg. 9, 35</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">calvariae locus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Matt. 27, 33</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">of beasts: canis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					30, 6, 18, § 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equae, asinae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. 1, 35, 16</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			eccl. Lat., <i>Calvary</i>, <i>the place
				where Jesus Christ was crucified</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 3, 198</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
